{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 36, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a movie that tells the story of the founding of facebook and the subsequent lawsuits that followed. the film is directed by david fincher and written by aaron sorkin, who is known for his quick-witted dialogue and engaging storylines. the movie stars jesse eisenberg as mark zuckerberg, the founder of facebook, and andrew garfield as eduardo saverin, zuckerberg's friend and business partner.\n\nthe movie begins with mark zuckerberg, a harvard undergraduate, creating a website called facemash, which allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. the site becomes popular, but also generates controversy and gets zuckerberg into trouble with the university. later, zuckerberg is approached by cameron and tyler winklevoss, two harvard students who have an idea for a social networking site exclusively for harvard students. zuckerberg agrees to help them, but eventually drops the project and creates his own site, which he calls thefacebook.\n\nas thefacebook gains popularity, zuckerberg becomes increasingly obsessed with the site and begins to push away his friends and acquaintances. he also becomes involved in a series of lawsuits, including one with the winklevoss twins, who claim that zuckerberg stole their idea, and another with eduardo saverin, who claims that zuckerberg unfairly diluted his shares in the company.\n\nthe movie is well-acted, with eisenberg giving a particularly strong performance as the socially awkward and intensely focused zuckerberg. the film also features a strong supporting cast, including justin timberlake as sean parker, the co-founder of napster, and rooney mara as erica albright, zuckerberg's girlfriend.\n\none of the strengths of the movie is its ability to balance the technical details of the facebook story with the more personal and emotional aspects of the c